139,19f1f512703269f5,"Wed, 01 Jul 2026 20:13:59 +0000 (UTC)",Conduent <TalentAcquisition@jobalerts.conduent.com>,Thank You,"Dear Netanya,Thank you for your interest in employment with&nbsp;Conduent.After reviewing your resume and considering your qualifications, we have decided to pursue other candidates who better match the qualifications for this position. We encourage you to visit our website and apply for new positions as they become available.&nbsp;We appreciate your interest in our company and wish you success in your career search.Regards,ConduentBeware of work-from-home job scams from criminals posing as Conduent recruiters.Here are signs of impersonation to look out for:Email that does not come from an Conduent.com email address.Conduent recruiters do not use personal email accounts such as Gmail or yahoo for official business.&nbsp; Also be aware of misspellings of Conduent in the email addressRequests for interviews over Skype, IM, Facebook Chat, or other social media messaging apps.&nbsp; Conduent recruiters will always communicate with official Conduent.com email, talk to you directly over the phone or send you an SMS to remind you of the next steps in the recruitment processConduent will never ask you to deposit checks, provide bank account information, or purchase equipment as part of the interview processIf you have any concerns about communications from recruiters claiming to be from Conduent, please don’t hesitate to verify by contacting Conduent HR at:&nbsp;recruitmentcontactcenter@conduent.comConnect With us onCopyrights 2026, ConduentTo ensure delivery to your inbox, please add TalentAcquisition@jobalerts.conduent.com to your address bookYou can unsubscribe here and stop receiving these job alert emails

